                                "The dashboard does not allow editing the briefing content -- it simply opens the existing file for display. " +
                                "Typical PDF content includes: safety topics, quality hold or alert notices, customer requirements, " +
                                "production targets, process or equipment updates, and shift handover notes. " +
                                "Contact your section owner if the briefing content needs to be updated.",
                                "#22c55e"); }

                            <div style="color:#e8f4f8; font-size:11px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:8px;">STEP-BY-STEP</div>

                            <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; margin-bottom:14px;">
                                <div style="background:#060d1f; border:1px solid #1a3a5c; border-radius:10px; padding:10px 14px; display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:10px;">
                                    <div style="width:20px; height:20px; border-radius:50%; background:#22c55e22; border:1px solid #22c55e44; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0; margin-top:1px;">
                                        <span style="color:#22c55e; font-size:9px; font-weight:700;">1</span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div style="color:#7ab3cc; font-size:11px; line-height:1.6;">Launch the dashboard from the configure screen. The toolbar appears at the bottom of the screen.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div style="background:#060d1f; border:1px solid #1a3a5c; border-radius:10px; padding:10px 14px; display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:10px;">
                                    <div style="width:20px; height:20px; border-radius:50%; background:#22c55e22; border:1px solid #22c55e44; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0; margin-top:1px;">
                                        <span style="color:#22c55e; font-size:9px; font-weight:700;">2</span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div style="color:#7ab3cc; font-size:11px; line-height:1.6;">Click the <span style="color:#22c55e; font-weight:700;">BRIEFING</span> button (megaphone icon) in the toolbar. The briefing dialog opens.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div style="background:#060d1f; border:1px solid #1a3a5c; border-radius:10px; padding:10px 14px; display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:10px;">
                                    <div style="width:20px; height:20px; border-radius:50%; background:#22c55e22; border:1px solid #22c55e44; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0; margin-top:1px;">
                                        <span style="color:#22c55e; font-size:9px; font-weight:700;">3</span>
                                    </div>
                                    <div style="color:#7ab3cc; font-size:11px; line-height:1.6;">Read through all the briefing content. Scroll down if there are multiple items or sections.</div>
                                </div>
                                <div style="background:#060d1f; border:1px solid #1a3a5c; border-radius:10px; padding:10px 14px; display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:10px;">
                                    <div style="width:20px; height:20px; border-radius:50%; background:#22c55e22; border:1px solid #22c55e44; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0; margin-top:1px;">
